+    Apply a suite of filters to a collection of examples.
+
+    Returns a tuple ``(kept, dropped)`` where ``kept`` is the list of examples
+    that passed all filters and ``dropped`` is a ``Counter`` mapping filter names
+    to the number of examples they rejected.
